## Project Structure

```
.
├── docker-compose.yml
├── backend/src
│   ├── server.ts      # Express app, Bull Board, boot reconciliation
│   ├── worker.ts      # BullMQ worker: claim, rate limit, send
│   ├── queue.ts       # Queue + idempotent job creation
│   ├── routes.ts      # REST API
│   ├── auth.ts        # Google + Slack OAuth
│   ├── mailer.ts      # Ethereal senders + SMTP
│   ├── search.ts      # Elasticsearch
│   ├── slack.ts       # Slack notifications
│   ├── db.ts / redis.ts / config.ts
└── frontend/src
    ├── components/    # ui, EmailTable, ComposeModal, Header
    ├── pages/         # Login, Dashboard
    ├── hooks/         # useAuth
    ├── lib/           # format helpers
    └── api.ts / types.ts
```

---

## Assumptions and Trade-offs
- Fixed hourly windows rather than a sliding window.
- Bull Board is behind login but not role-restricted.
- Failed sends retry 3 times with exponential backoff, then show as `failed`.
- Redis AOF is enabled; if Redis data is lost entirely, jobs are rebuilt from Postgres on the next server boot.
- UI is built from the assignment spec; spacing and colors may differ slightly from the Figma.
